This is what I suggest.

"Puerto Rican Independence Party" is three concepts: "Puerto Rican"
"Independence" and "Party". So, I would make that three names, not one,
although independence and party are probably better as normal sumti valsi.

Anyway, here's what I got:

Puerto Rico : la bloti marbi me'e lu ricfu cu gugde
independence : lo zifre
party : lo jecta girzu

We can take this and form lujvo out of it to make it nicer to say:

Puerto Rico : la blomrame'ecfu gugde (Wow, that's long)
(shortened) : la blomracfu
party : lo jecgri

So then we have

lo la blomracfu ku jecgri cu sarji lo zifre

And if you really want a cmene:

la blomracfuzi'ejecgri (Not very pretty, I'd say, but pronouncable.)

OR (zo'o.ui) la'o gy. Peurto Rican Independence Party .gy.

Anyway, there's my two cents. Enjoy!

